3734	                // by owner ruling after 08ff51a33e demoted it.
3735	                //
3736	                // THE DEMOTION'S ARGUMENT AND WHY IT WAS REJECTED. It ran: how
3737	                // many times this branch is reached depends on when the host
3738	                // delivers a child's final wait status, that is an external
3739	                // real-time event, an INFO line driven by one is a determinism
3740	                // hazard by construction, so keep the loop sub-INFO. The
3741	                // measurement offered with it was real -- over 312 concurrent
3742	                // SaBRe cell-runs, 4 diverged, and in each the whole difference
3743	                // was this line plus one unrelated WARN.
3744	                //
3745	                // The owner's ruling: this fizzle is part of the deterministic
3746	                // scheduling model, not record/replay external-IO terrain, so it
3747	                // SHOULD be a deterministic function of detcore scheduling. If it
3748	                // is not, that is a hermit DEFECT, and demoting the line hid the
3749	                // defect instead of fixing it. The previous note ended "do not
3750	                // promote this back without making the host's wait-status
